A||||6||88 Fiero||I hear ya Ozzy!!!
Z||000000||88 Fiero||09-05-99||10:04 PM||||It's really nice to know that there are people out there that dedicate their talents in restoring this car....My freind Keith Huff who is the owner of Fiero Motorsports in Anaheim, CA...he's been working Fiero's since 1984. He is very knowlegeable from engine conversion such as the V8's, Quad 4's,modified 2.8's to punch out's 2.8 to 3.1 or 3.2, to coversions to 3.4's. Also any problems that you are experiencing whether it's suspension or overheating problem, he can tell you. I used to remember back then in the '80's on how him and his Dad would go out in the Fiero Assembly Plant and talk to the designers and engineering people of this car... and try to get as much info that everybody can benefit in insuring that this car can go on forever....Right now in his possession which is an ongoing project of another Fiero enthusiast is a 1988 Fiero GT which has the 3.4 block water cooled turbo system... This is not a Design One turbo...the car has a modified automatic tranny and can leave a 6 foot skid mark...His Dad Fiero Phil of FOCOA also have in his show room a Black '88 Fiero GT with the Gary Zumalt V8 kit and an LT1 corvette engine...and this car is very, very wicked....Oh...I forgot...John Parenti also works at Fiero Motorsport...you've gotta see this guys car...'85 GT and it has the Ford Probe Green Color with a modified 3800 engine in it...anyway..if you need help here is their phone no. 714-639-9005.
Z||000001||Ozzy||09-05-99||11:01 PM||||Yeah man... I wus chekin' their site last night and thinking of joining their membership. I see they discount parts to members which is cool. (If lowCG would get back to me I'm thinkin of tryin to get somethin similar goin in the Northwest.) But I'm hesitant because they come across with a bit too much LA attitude on the web site. Although the fee is not much, if I'm gonna pay it, I wan't from them what they say they do. Are they too busy to answer my questions (and I do have a lot) without getting pissy? <br> <br>I am yet to call them so I will chek 'em out soon. Now do they deal with the basic putt putt Fiero dude like me with a MASSIVE power plant like the 'Iron Duck'? I'm a long way off from putting a V10 in my Fiero but I am enthusiastic about it just the same. I just want folks who take the time to give me straight, accurate advice to lead me in the right direction and I always remember them and turn others onto them, and one day might want to transplant a Rolls Royce jet turbine into my lil' Fiero and I'll have them do it!<p>Ozzy<p>
Z||000002||lowCG||09-06-99||01:35 AM||||Did I miss something?<br>There's a club here called<br>"Jet City Fieros",I got a card here somewhere, from some nice people at the Northwest vintage races last month.<br>Been too busy looking for a job,and tinkering with the car whenever I can to even have a chance to check out their organization,however.They're not online,and meet once a month for pizza,a good ways North of here,I understand.
Z||000003||88 Fiero||09-06-99||07:32 AM||||Ozzy...Keith is a pretty cool guy tho'..known him since the introduction of the Fiero...just let him know that Gabe put a plug for him here in the forum...If you want to put a V6 Fiero in exchange for a 4 cylinder he can help you...If you need anything let me know and I will find that out for you...If you want the 3.4 block out of a camaro he could set you one up ready to be assembled to the top end of the 2.8 block...it will look stock but you can tell the difference when you accelerate...he got one on his car with headers and it moves...the good thing about the 3.4 is that the block is ribbed for strength and durability...which makes it a good candidate for a turbo unit...let say 12 lbs. of boost....he he he 
Z||000004||Ozzy||09-06-99||09:54 AM||||Hey guys. <p>lowCG...is your e-mail address still current? I sent you a message several days ago. Basically I was asking if there were any clubs up there because I'm about to move to your area. I'm also trying to think of ways to get shop pricing on parts. I know a rep down here for Carquest who has done me some favors. If there was enough Fieros up there something could be started and I wanted to know if you were interested. If not thats cool to. Can't do much without money / job... Maybe we can have coffee sometime and jaw about Fiero's sometime.<p>Hey 88 fiero...thanks man I appreciate the feedback. As I said, I'm a little ways off transplanting engines into this thing. Gonna get all the life outta this little beast first. I really want to get all the suspension and handling right at the moment and make sure I'm squeezing every horse possible from 'The little engine that could'!<p>Ozzy<p>
